# Content — where models are loaded from.
#
# Both are optional. With neither set the scene renders its procedural
# placeholder and makes no network request.
#
# VITE_CONTENT_BASE_URL is the host serving content. Unset, `resolveAssetUrl`
# resolves paths against the app's own origin (i.e. `public/`).
# VITE_MODEL_PATH is the object path of the model to display.
#
# The values below load a Kenney ambulance (CC0) from the Onklave asset library:
#
# VITE_CONTENT_BASE_URL=https://assets.onklave.app
# VITE_MODEL_PATH=kenney/3.6.0/car-kit/ambulance.glb
#
# Vite bakes VITE_* variables at BUILD time, so setting these in the deployed
# container does nothing — they must be present when `npm run build` runs. The
# platform has no build-time env surface today (onklave.yaml carries runtime
# port/health/command/resources only), so an app that needs a content host
# commits it in `.env.production`. Fine for a public CDN host; do NOT put a
# secret in a VITE_ variable — it ends up in the JS bundle either way.
